More Vulnerabilities That Can Be Paid (211–220)
211. Privilege Escalation
Privilege Escalation
A user with limited privileges gains higher-level permissions such as admin access.
💰 Typical payout: $1,000 – $15,000
212. Account Takeover via Password Reset
Account Takeover
Weak password reset logic allows attackers to take control of accounts.
💰 Typical payout: $1,000 – $15,000
213. OAuth Token Replay Attack
OAuth Token Replay
Attackers reuse previously issued OAuth tokens to gain unauthorized access.
💰 Typical payout: $500 – $7,000
214. Improper Rate Limiting
Rate Limiting Bypass
Applications fail to properly limit requests, enabling brute-force attacks.
💰 Typical payout: $200 – $3,000
215. Session Fixation
Session Fixation
Attackers force victims to use a known session ID to hijack accounts.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $5,000
216. Token Prediction Attack
Token Prediction
Security tokens are predictable due to weak generation algorithms.
💰 Typical payout: $500 – $8,000
217. Email Spoofing via Application
Email Spoofing
Applications allow sending emails that appear to come from trusted sources.
💰 Typical payout: $200 – $3,000
218. Unauthorized Data Export
Unauthorized Data Export
Export functions allow downloading sensitive information without proper checks.
💰 Typical payout: $500 – $8,000
219. Weak Password Policy
Weak Password Policy
Applications allow extremely weak passwords that increase risk of compromise.
💰 Typical payout: $50 – $500
220. Improper API Authentication
Improper API Authentication
APIs fail to verify authentication properly, allowing unauthorized requests.
💰 Typical payout: $500 – $8,000
